# The cross toolchain of LFS chapters 5 and 6, which the other lists do not
# carry.
#
# wget-list-core and wget-list-gui describe the system that gets installed.
# These five describe the compiler that installs it, and they are separate
# because they are the only tarballs here that never reach the image: the
# chapter 5 toolchain lands in $LFS/tools and chapter 7.13 deletes it.
#
# glibc-2.42 and glibc-2.42-fhs-1.patch are not listed. They are already in
# sources/ for packages/glibc.sh, and chapter 5 builds that same tarball --
# once cross-compiled into $LFS, and again natively in chapter 8.
#
# gmp, mpfr and mpc are GCC's arithmetic dependencies. They are not built as
# packages; they unpack *inside* the gcc tree under those exact names and
# GCC's build system picks them up on its own (LFS 5.3.1).
# The kernel is here for its headers only, and the version matters. See
# toolchain/linux-headers.sh: glibc 2.42 will not compile against the 7.x
# uapi headers in src/linux.
https://www.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/linux-6.16.1.tar.xz
https://sourceware.org/pub/binutils/releases/binutils-2.45.tar.xz
https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/gcc/gcc-15.2.0/gcc-15.2.0.tar.xz
https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/gmp/gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz
https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/mpfr/mpfr-4.2.2.tar.xz
https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/mpc/mpc-1.3.1.tar.gz

# Chapter 6, the temporary tools. Most of that chapter's packages are already
# in wget-list-core -- bash, coreutils, sed, grep, gawk, findutils, diffutils,
# gzip, tar and xz are all in the image too, and chapter 6 builds the same
# tarballs -- so only what the console system does not already need is here.
#
# m4, file, make and patch are build tools rather than parts of the image.
# They are in chapter 6 because chapter 8 cannot be built without them, and
# chapter 7.13 deletes the temporary copies once the real ones exist.
https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/m4/m4-1.4.20.tar.xz
https://astron.com/pub/file/file-5.46.tar.gz
https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/make/make-4.4.1.tar.gz
https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/patch/patch-2.8.tar.xz

# ncurses, and not the 6.5 release that wget-list-core carries.
#
# The book uses this dated snapshot and chapter 6 configures it
# --with-cxx-shared. Plain 6.5 does not build its C++ binding under gcc 15 --
# packages/ncurses.sh has the details and drops the binding with
# --without-cxx-binding to get around it -- and the snapshot is where that is
# fixed. Two different tarballs of the same version is unfortunate; building
# the book's chapter with a package the book does not describe is worse.
#
# From the LFS package mirror rather than the URL the book prints. Upstream
# publishes snapshots under archives/ncurses/current/, and "current" means
# what it says: 20250809 has already rotated out of it and that URL is a 404,
# which is how this entry failed the first time it was fetched. The mirror
# pins the exact set of tarballs LFS 12.4 was released against, so it does not
# move. If osuosl is ever unreachable the same file is on any LFS mirror under
# lfs-packages/12.4/.
https://ftp.osuosl.org/pub/lfs/lfs-packages/12.4/ncurses-6.5-20250809.tgz

# Chapter 7, built inside the chroot. util-linux is already in wget-list-core;
# these five are not in the image at all.
#
# They are the tools chapter 8's packages are configured and built *by* --
# perl and python run configure scripts and generate sources, bison and
# gettext are what half of GNU is written against, texinfo builds the info
# pages -- rather than programs the finished system needs. Chapter 7.13
# deletes /tools around them; these stay, and chapter 8 rebuilds them properly.
https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/gettext/gettext-0.26.tar.xz
https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/bison/bison-3.8.2.tar.xz
https://www.cpan.org/src/5.0/perl-5.42.0.tar.xz
https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.13.7/Python-3.13.7.tar.xz
https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/texinfo/texinfo-7.2.tar.xz
